  <prompt>Four client test suites are red or silently mis-configured on master. Make each one test the real behaviour again, without changing production code unless a test exposes a real production defect (then stop and report it).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE front-end engineer. A test that cannot fail, or cannot run, is worse than none.</role>
  <goal>On master + this PR: the four packages' jest runs pass, every previously failing test either passes against current behaviour or is rewritten/deleted with an ADR-038 reason, and no test passes only because it exercises a mock of the code under test.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
#1416: src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/test/emailShareDraft.test.ts:34 fails; the package mock test/__mocks__/spaarke-ui-components.tsx:166 defines cleanGuid as identity, the real one strips braces.
#1417: src/solutions/SmartTodo/jest.config.cjs:16 uses setupFilesAfterEach (not a Jest option; Jest warns "Unknown option"), so jest.setup.cjs never loads; the key is setupFilesAfterEnv.
#1388: src/solutions/WorkspaceLayoutWizard: 14 tests fail in src/__tests__/rowHeight.test.tsx (looks for data-testid row-height-dropdown-*; ArrangeStep.tsx:901 now renders row-height-dropdown-popover-*) and sectionInstanceAdvanced.test.tsx (advanced-accordion-* no longer rendered), after the 2026-07-03 R2 UAT rework (708f18bb75, 803c77ace1).
#1392: src/client/pcf/SemanticSearchControl: 9 of 11 suites fail: component suites cannot load `scheduler` (React 16 peer under jest); hook suites (useFilters, useInfiniteScroll, useSemanticSearch, useSemanticSearch.searchIndexName) and resolveSearchIndexNameAsync are stale; resolveSearchIndexNameAsync needs generated/ManifestTypes (build output: run scripts/Invoke-PcfBuildProd.ps1 first). Repro commands are in each issue.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/test/__mocks__/spaarke-ui-components.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/SmartTodo/jest.config.cjs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/WorkspaceLayoutWizard/src/__tests__/rowHeight.test.tsx, sectionInstanceAdvanced.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/pcf/SemanticSearchControl/jest.config.js, jest.setup.ts, package.json (devDependency only), SemanticSearchControl/**/__tests__/*</file>
      <file role="read">docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md, docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: test files, jest config and test-only devDependencies in the four packages. Production source changes are out of scope; if a test reveals a production defect, STOP for that suite and report it (it becomes a task) instead of bending the test.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">#1416: the mock must use the real cleanGuid (import the real implementation, or map that export to the real module), not a hand-written copy. #1417: after the rename, run the suite; fix any test that relied on the setup not loading. #1388 and #1392: update each test to the current UI/hook contract, or delete and rewrite it under ADR-038 build-vs-maintain; record the decision per test file in the PR body. Never skip (.skip / xit) a failing test to get green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">NEW worktree off origin/master (git worktree add C:\wts-128 -b fix/client-test-harness-128 origin/master); own PR; do not merge. Install with npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund. PCF build via scripts/Invoke-PcfBuildProd.ps1 (judge by output). If PR #1415 (task 111, SemanticSearchControl) is open, do not bump the PCF version and expect to rebase. Never use --no-verify or bare git stash. You cannot write .claude/.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor; read ADR-038 and TEST-ARCHITECTURE.</step>
    <step order="1">Reproduce each issue on origin/master; record counts.</step>
    <step order="2">Fix #1416 and #1417; run both packages.</step>
    <step order="3">Fix #1388 and #1392 per test file (update vs rewrite vs delete, with reason).</step>
    <step order="4">Run all four packages' suites; code-review and adr-check (testing tag); PR with before/after counts; do not merge.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Daily Briefing: emailShareDraft.test.ts passes using the real cleanGuid; the package suite has no failures.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SmartTodo: jest prints no "Unknown option" warning, jest.setup.cjs is loaded (a test relying on it passes), and the suite has no failures.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">WorkspaceLayoutWizard and SemanticSearchControl: jest has no failing or unloadable suite; each changed or deleted test file has its ADR-038 reason in the PR body; the FR-02 row-height and FR-03 Advanced-panel behaviours each keep at least one assertion against the current UI.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">PR open against master with before/after counts per package; Closes #1416, #1417, #1388, #1392.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no production source file changed; no test skipped; no PCF version bump. Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Created 2026-10-08 by the no-parking sweep (D-81 rule). #1416/#1417 were filed by task 106 (ISS-015, ISS-016); #1388/#1392 by task 056.</notes>

